# Export rules for the public snapshot sync.
#
# .gitignore has NO effect on files that are already tracked. These
# export-ignore rules are what actually keep internal files out of the curated
# public snapshot, so anything built with `git archive` cannot leak them by
# accident.
#
# Kept out of the public repo:
#   .gitea/        this instance's CI, useless (and noise) off-site
#   .github/       does not exist yet; create it local-only once GitHub CI is
#                  wanted, and delete this line at the same time
#
# Everything else IS published, including docker-compose.yml and
# pi-sandbox.Dockerfile — they are the actual deployment examples.
.gitea/                        export-ignore
.github/                       export-ignore
.gitignore                     export-ignore
# The internal CA chain. Kept in the repo because pi-sandbox builds with it, but
# EXCLUDED from the public snapshot: it is a trust anchor for a private namespace
# and has no meaning off-site. A grep for the hostname cannot see inside a PEM, so
# excluding it here is the only thing that keeps it out.
nuc-ca-chain.pem               export-ignore
.dockerignore                  export-ignore
